[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
If you want to finish setting up AIDE, don't forget to customise your
own aide.conf in %%PREFIX%%/etc/aide.conf. You will also need to run
the following commands:

	cd /var/db/aide
	aide --init
	mv databases/aide.db.new databases/aide.db

You may want to change the permissions of the /var/db/aide/ directory tree.

For your reference, a copy of the original aide.conf is supplied in
%%PREFIX%%/etc/aide.conf.sample.
EOM
}
{ type: upgrade
  maximum_version: 0.18.8
  message: <<EOM
AIDE 0.19 is not backwards compatible with 0.18 configurations and
databases. Before running aide after this upgrade, review
%%PREFIX%%/etc/aide.conf (see aide.conf(5)):

  - 'database' is no longer supported; rename it to 'database_in'
  - 'summarize_changes' is now 'report_summarize_changes'
  - 'grouped' is now 'report_grouped'
  - the tiger, haval, crc32, crc32b and whirlpool hashsums were
    removed; drop them from rules (e.g. R-tiger-rmd160-sha1 -> R)
  - md5, sha1, rmd160 and gost are deprecated
  - the default R group now uses sha3_256 instead of md5
  - unrestricted negative rules (!<regex>) now recurse into matching
    directories; use the new '-<regex>' rules to prune them
  - rules now apply only to file system entries

Check the configuration with 'aide --config-check', then
re-initialize the database:

	aide --init
	mv /var/db/aide/databases/aide.db.new /var/db/aide/databases/aide.db
EOM
}
]
